        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T13:41:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the AARect renderstep, I used an outset of 1px for the vertex placement, and then could adjust what the interpolated target value was depending on the stroke width (-1/2 if we weren\u0027t subpixel and really did only want a 1/2px outset, or 0 if we were subpixel/hairline and wanted a 2px wide strip of geometry to better hit pixels).\n\nI don\u0027t think it\u0027s worth changing anything now necessarily, particularly if we adjust to having arcs handled in the aarect renderstep, which we then get this handling for free. But I wanted to raise it if it had any impacts on the vertex structure of this technique or of your future ideas.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 233,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 233,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "c78a405c229e185314e2bfda6b16f10579b25a78",
